## UK Dental Marketing Statistics 2026 (Quick Answer)

- There is no measured UK search volume for "dental marketing statistics" or close variants. This page exists as a sourced reference for dental practices and referral partners, not a keyword-volume play (Ahrefs, checked September 2026)
- The GDC register held **47,022** dentists as of January 2026, up **3.2%** on the 45,580 recorded a year earlier (General Dental Council, 2026)
- The share of England's roughly **10,160** dental practices offering NHS general dentistry has fallen from **64.6%** in 2017 to **55.6%** in 2026, and the NHS has lost at least 600 practices holding a general contract over that period (Nuffield Trust, 2026)
- Only **38%** of people seeking a new NHS dental appointment get one, against **87%** for returning patients, and overall NHS dental activity sits **8%** below pre-Covid levels (Nuffield Trust, citing the 2025 GP Patient Survey)
- No independently sourced UK figure exists for how dental patients split between search, referral, and walk-in, or for a dental-specific patient acquisition cost. Every version of those numbers this page checked traced back to a marketing agency's own page with no named study behind it
- Local Pack click-through data (general local business, not dental-specific) shows position 1 taking **17.8%** of clicks, position 2 **13.6%**, position 3 **10.4%** (BrightLocal, Backlinko, 2026)

